ID: vr-65
Title: Shared model-aware presentation and native MPFB feature parity

Status: DONE
Milestone: Consistent native speaking heads
Dependencies: vr-44, vr-49, vr-57, vr-58

Purpose:
  Give the original native MPFB head the shared player's full presentation,
  framing, neck, hair, colors, cursor, zoom and blinking controls without
  substituting Claire geometry or loading inactive models.

Tasks:
  Share the packed geometry/rendering contract with explicit native calibration.
  Preserve native MPFB rest/topology and its actual neural motion transfer.
  Apply neutral-relative exaggeration after native fitting, with honest limits.
  Promote the reviewed sideways-cheekiness cue into a bounded shared option.
  Qualify actual controls, geometry restoration, cancellation and resources.
  Update the implementation chapters, index and causal development ledger.

Acceptance criteria:
  Native MPFB exposes the same applicable live controls as Claire in browser
    and desktop sessions; all four face presentations work.
  Native shape remains distinct; transforms are documented and reversible.
  Two/four-times exaggeration acts on the native output rather than merely
    labeling an amplified source subsequently clipped to a bounded rig.
  Cosmetic cheekiness remains distinguishable from learned emotion/accuracy.
  Only the selected model/adapter and active presentation resources load.
  Existing live Claire and sibling sessions remain untouched.

Completion evidence:
  Shared packed native renderer supports all four presentations and applicable
    Claire controls. Native MPFB geometry/transfer remain distinct; final
    neutral-relative exaggeration follows bounded intermediate fitting.
  88 CPU regressions and focused hairstyle checks pass. Actual six-model native
    sessions03 and final actual MPFB WebGL color/blink/cheekiness/resource
    checks pass. Hair fit is one-time, both styles use the same calibration.
  Selected-only engine probes and exact six-model GIF timelines are retained.
    No anatomical/listening/identity approval or universal lifecycle claim.
  GitHub: https://github.com/Zanark/Verona/issues/64

Completion log:
  2026-11-21 - Owner explicitly requests full native MPFB/Mark parity and a
    performance-conscious implementation. Existing MPFB has a separate reduced
    renderer and bounded native fit; sideways-smirk prior art is report-only.
    Protect the currently loaded Claire/Hazel instance; use owned test lanes.
  2026-11-21 - Implemented and environment-qualified. Owner authorized pausing
    this chat's head/empty manager, preserving settings for updated restart.
    Failed lifecycle/media receipts remain; delivery continues under vr-67.
